{"url": "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4729284", "title": "A Profitable Day Trading Strategy For The U.S. Equity Market", "engine": "exa", "published": "N/A", "snippet": "# A Profitable Day Trading Strategy For The U.S. Equity Market\n...\nSwiss Finance Institute Research Paper No. 24-98\n27 PagesPosted: 15 Mar 2024Last revised: 26 Nov 2024\nSee all articles by Carlo Zarattini**## Carlo Zarattini\n...\nConcretum Group\n...\n## Andrea Barbon\n...\nUniversity of St. Gallen; University of St.Gallen\n...\n## Andrew Aziz\nPeak Capital Trading; Bear Bull Traders\nDate Written: February 16, 2024\n...\nThe validity of day trading as a long-term consistent and uncorrelated source of income for traders and investors is a matter of debate. In this paper, we endeavored to answer this question by conducting a thorough analysis of the profitability of Opening Range Breakout (ORB) strategies, with a particular focus on the 5-minute ORB. Using a large dataset that covered more than 7,000 US stocks traded from 2016 to 2023, the research aimed to assess how eﬀective this strategy was in producing consistent and uncorrelated returns. A new aspect of our study was the focus on Stocks in Play, which are stocks that show higher than normal trading activity on a specific day, mostly because of fundamental news about the company. Our results showed a significant benefit in limiting day trading only to those Stocks in Play (even after considering transaction costs). A portfolio that consisted of the top 20 Stocks in Play achieved a total net performance of over 1,600%, with a Sharpe ratio of 2.81, and an annualized alpha of 36%. Passive exposure in the S&P 500 would have achieved a t", "extra": {}, "read_via": "exa_fetch", "text_chars": 5479, "excerpt": "# A Profitable Day Trading Strategy For The U.S. Equity Market URL: https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4729284 A Profitable Day Trading Strategy For The U.S. Equity Market by Carlo Zarattini, Andrea Barbon, Andrew Aziz :: SSRN Skip to main content ** ** PDF iconDownload This Paper Open PDF in Browser **Add Paper to My Library Share: * ** * ** * ** * ** Permalink Using these links ", "jev": {"concrete": 0.67, "evidence": "backtest", "evidence_confidence": 0.99, "market": "us_stocks_etfs", "us_long_only": 0.75, "recent": 0.95, "code": 0.07}, "priority": 0.601}
{"url": "https://quantmacro.substack.com/p/paper-review-an-effective-intraday", "title": "Paper Review: An Effective Intraday Momentum Strategy", "engine": "exa", "published": "2025-03-14", "snippet": "### A paper by Zarrattini, Aziz, Barbon\n...\nLink to paper: Beat the Market An Effective Intraday Momentum Strategy for S&P500 ETF (SPY) by Carlo Zarattini, Andrew Aziz, Andrea Barbon. Swiss Finance Institute Research Paper No. 24-97\n...\nI came across this paper recently and decided to give it a read. I had looked into Opening Range Breakout (ORB) type strategies in the past, which were classic breakouts that were developed by the likes of Crabel, decades ago. There is still a typewritten pdf file talking about that stuff somewhere on the internet.\n...\nThis paper is a fresh take on the ORB strategy, although the results are a bit too good to be true. I will first talk about what I like about the paper, then have a few constructive critiques about it. In no ways this is a summary of the paper, interested readers should read the paper itself.\n...\nThe breakout strategy they use can be described as a way to define a “noise band”, where the noise is related to the volatility of returns from Open until time T, on a given day:\n...\nThe novelty of this relatively simple way of calculating VSO using historical intraday returns is that it takes into account the intraday seasonality of volatility. One should expect higher volatility during open and going into the close, with a lower volatility during mid-day. This results in an intuitively meaningful noise cone, where the cone ramps up quickly near the open where there is high market volatility, then slows down, and into the close it ramp", "extra": {}, "read_via": "direct", "text_chars": 5591, "excerpt": "Link to paper: Beat the Market An Effective Intraday Momentum Strategy for S&P500 ETF (SPY) by Carlo Zarattini, Andrew Aziz, Andrea Barbon. Swiss Finance Institute Research Paper No. 24-97 I came across this paper recently and decided to give it a read. I had looked into Opening Range Breakout (ORB) type strategies in the past, which were classic breakouts that were developed by the likes of Crabe", "jev": {"concrete": 0.8, "evidence": "backtest", "evidence_confidence": 0.81, "market": "us_stocks_etfs", "us_long_only": 0.67, "recent": 0.4, "code": 0.04}, "priority": 0.581}
{"url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/carlozarattini_backtesting-the-opening-range-breakout-orb-activity-7305637543012675585-ZVhw", "title": "We are excited to announce that we have just published the Python code to replicate our most-read paper, \"Can Day Trading Really Be Profitable?\", co-authored with Andrew Aziz in 2023 and read … | Carlo Zarattini", "engine": "exa", "published": "2025-03-12", "snippet": "# We are excited to announce that we have just published the Python code to replicate our most-read paper, \"Can Day Trading Really Be Profitable?\", co-authored with Andrew Aziz in 2023 and read … | Carlo Zarattini · LinkedIn · 2025-03-12\n...\nWe are excited to announce that we have just published the Python code to replicate our most-read paper, \"Can Day Trading Really Be Profitable?\", co-authored with Andrew Aziz in 2023 and read by more than 30,000 people.\n...\nThis code allows users—even those with no programming experience—to backtest the 5-minute Opening Range Breakout strategy on different tickers or with alternative position management approaches.\n...\nWhile the model described in the paper has shown profitability, it is far from being a fully developed trading system. Incorporating filters to avoid trading in noisy market conditions can significantly improve the hit ratio and profitability while reducing trading costs—we leave this challenge to the most ambitious traders.\n\n---", "extra": {}, "read_via": "direct", "text_chars": 16547, "excerpt": "We are excited to announce that we have just published the Python code to replicate our most-read paper, \"Can Day Trading Really Be Profitable?\", co-authored with Andrew Aziz in 2023 and read by more than 30,000 people. This code allows users—even those with no programming experience—to backtest the 5-minute Opening Range Breakout strategy on different tickers or with alternative position manageme", "jev": {"concrete": 0.75, "evidence": "backtest", "evidence_confidence": 0.76, "market": "other", "us_long_only": 0.66, "recent": 0.84, "code": 0.59}, "priority": 0.544}
{"url": "https://concretumgroup.com/a-profitable-day-trading-strategy-for-the-u-s-equity-market/", "title": "A Profitable Day Trading Strategy For The U.S. Equity Market", "engine": "exa", "published": "2024-04-26", "snippet": "Authors: Carlo Zarattini, Andrea Barbon, Andrew Aziz\n...\nResearch paper examining the profitability of the Opening Range Breakout day trading strategy.\n...\nThe Opening Range Breakout (ORB) strategy is a popular intraday trading method that attempts to capture strong price movements immediately after the market opens. This research paper evaluates whether such a day trading strategy can generate consistent and risk-adjusted returns in U.S. equity markets.\n...\nTo evaluate the effectiveness of the ORB trading strategy, we analyze a dataset containing more than 7,000 U.S. stocks traded between 2016 and 2023.\n...\nThe study focuses primarily on the 5-minute Opening Range Breakout, while also comparing alternative time frames such as 15-minute, 30-minute, and 60-minute opening ranges.\n...\n## Stocks in Play and Day Trading Opportunities\n...\nA key contribution of this research is the focus on Stocks in Play. These are stocks experiencing unusually high trading activity due to company-specific news, earnings announcements, or other fundamental developments.\n...\nBy restricting trades to these highly active securities, the strategy significantly improves performance even after accounting for transaction costs.\n...\nThe results demonstrate strong performance for the ORB day trading strategy.\n...\nA portfolio consisting of the top 20 Stocks in Play achieved:\n...\n• More than 1,600% total net return• Sharpe ratio of 2.81• Annualized alpha of 36%\n...\nThe research also compares ORB strategies us", "extra": {}, "read_via": "direct", "text_chars": 2387, "excerpt": "Opening Range Breakout (ORB) Day Trading Strategy The Opening Range Breakout (ORB) strategy is a popular intraday trading method that attempts to capture strong price movements immediately after the market opens. This research paper evaluates whether such a day trading strategy can generate consistent and risk-adjusted returns in U.S. equity markets. Dataset and Research Methodology To evaluate th", "jev": {"concrete": 0.45, "evidence": "backtest", "evidence_confidence": 0.98, "market": "us_stocks_etfs", "us_long_only": 0.76, "recent": 0.88, "code": 0.06}, "priority": 0.393}
